45	12	Process improvement recommendations	ROLE:\nYou are a senior QA Lead / Test Manager specializing in quality process\nimprovement for Native iOS, Android, and web application delivery teams.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nTeam Structure: [e.g., 1 QA Lead + 3 QA Engineers + 1 SDET | Cross-functional squads]\nDevelopment Methodology: Agile | Scrum | Kanban | Waterfall | Hybrid\nImprovement Trigger: Retrospective finding | Escaped defect | Audit result |\n                     New QA Lead | Scaling team | [Other]\nCurrent Pain Points: [Brief description of the quality problems being experienced]\nImprovement Goal: [e.g., Reduce escaped defects | Faster feedback loops |\n                  Improve test coverage | Reduce regression time | [Other]]\n\nTASK:\nUsing the process assessment data and pain points provided below, produce a\nstructured set of quality process improvement recommendations.\n\nYou MUST cover ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Current state assessment — honest evaluation of where the process stands today\n  2. Root cause analysis — the underlying causes of each identified pain point\n  3. Improvement recommendations — specific, actionable changes with clear ownership\n  4. Prioritisation — recommendations ranked by impact and effort\n  5. Implementation roadmap — phased plan with timelines and milestones\n  6. Success metrics — how each improvement will be measured\n  7. Risks of change — what could go wrong during implementation\n  8. Quick wins — improvements deliverable within 1 sprint with high impact\n\nEvaluate ALL pain points before making any recommendation.\nEvery recommendation must address a specific root cause — not a symptom.\nDo NOT recommend generic best practices — every recommendation must be specific\nto the team size, methodology, and context stated above.\nIf assessment data is insufficient to diagnose root cause, flag as [NEEDS ASSESSMENT].\n\nPROCESS ASSESSMENT DATA AND PAIN POINTS:\n[Paste retrospective findings, defect analysis, team feedback, metrics data, and observations here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Recommendations must be realistic for the team size and capacity stated above\n- Root cause analysis must go at least 2 levels deep — symptom → cause → root cause\n- Implementation roadmap must fit within normal sprint cadence — no big-bang changes\n- Success metrics must be measurable before and after — not just "will feel better"\n- Quick wins must be genuinely achievable in 1 sprint — do not label complex changes as quick wins\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nPROCESS IMPROVEMENT RECOMMENDATIONS\nProject: [Name] | Team: [Structure] | Methodology: [Method]\nPrepared By: [QA Lead Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nImprovement Trigger: [Trigger stated in CONTEXT]\n\n---\n\n1. CURRENT STATE ASSESSMENT:\n| Process Area | Current State | Maturity Level | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Planning | [Description] | Ad hoc / Repeatable / Defined / Optimised | [Evidence from data] |\n| Test Design | [Description] | Ad hoc / Repeatable / Defined / Optimised | [Evidence] |\n| Defect Management | [Description] | Ad hoc / Repeatable / Defined / Optimised | [Evidence] |\n| Automation | [Description] | Ad hoc / Repeatable / Defined / Optimised | [Evidence] |\n| Reporting | [Description] | Ad hoc / Repeatable / Defined / Optimised | [Evidence] |\n| Shift-Left Practices | [Description] | Ad hoc / Repeatable / Defined / Optimised | [Evidence] |\n\nOverall Quality Maturity: Ad hoc | Repeatable | Defined | Optimised\nSummary: [2-3 sentences — honest overall assessment]\n\n---\n\n2. ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:\nPAIN POINT [N]: [Pain point title]\nSymptom: [What is observed — e.g., "High defect escape rate to production"]\nCause: [One level deeper — e.g., "Regression suite not covering recently changed areas"]\nRoot Cause: [Two levels deeper — e.g., "No process to update regression suite when features change"]\nImpact: High | Medium | Low\nEvidence: [Data or observation supporting this analysis]\n\n---\n(repeat for every pain point)\n\n---\n\n3. IMPROVEMENT RECOMMENDATIONS:\nRECOMMENDATION [N]:\nTitle: [Short descriptive title]\nAddresses: [Pain Point N — root cause stated above]\nDescription: [What specifically needs to change — concrete and actionable]\nOwner: [Role responsible for implementing]\nEffort: Low (≤1 sprint) | Medium (2-3 sprints) | High (>3 sprints)\nImpact: High | Medium | Low\nDependencies: [What must be true or done first — or "None"]\nImplementation Steps:\n  1. [Step]\n  2. [Step]\n  3. [Step]\n\n---\n(repeat for every recommendation)\n\n---\n\n4. PRIORITISATION MATRIX:\n| # | Recommendation | Impact | Effort | Priority | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Title] | High | Low | 🔴 Do first | [Why — high impact, low effort] |\n| 2 | [Title] | High | Medium | 🟡 Do next | [Why] |\n| 3 | [Title] | Medium | Low | 🟡 Do next | [Why] |\n| 4 | [Title] | Medium | High | 🟢 Plan in | [Why] |\n| 5 | [Title] | Low | High | ⚪ Defer | [Why] |\n\n---\n\n5. IMPLEMENTATION ROADMAP:\n| Phase | Sprint(s) | Recommendations | Milestone | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Phase 1 — Quick Wins | Sprint [N] | [Rec 1, Rec 2] | [Measurable milestone] | QA Lead |\n| Phase 2 — Core Fixes | Sprint [N+1] to [N+2] | [Rec 3, Rec 4] | [Measurable milestone] | QA Lead + Team |\n| Phase 3 — Optimise | Sprint [N+3] onwards | [Rec 5] | [Measurable milestone] | QA Lead |\n\n---\n\n6. SUCCESS METRICS:\n| Recommendation | Metric | Baseline | Target | Measurement Method | Review Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Rec 1 title] | [Metric] | [Current value] | [Target value] | [How measured] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| [Rec 2 title] | [Metric] | [Current value] | [Target value] | [How measured] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\n---\n\n7. RISKS OF CHANGE:\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Team resistance to new process | Medium | Medium | Involve team in design; explain the why before implementing |\n| Improvement slips during busy release period | High | Medium | Schedule Phase 1 outside release crunch; protect capacity |\n| New process adds overhead without immediate benefit | Medium | High | Define clear success metrics; review after 2 sprints and adjust |\n| [Additional risk] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Mitigation] |\n\n---\n\n8. QUICK WINS (deliverable within 1 sprint):\n| # | Quick Win | Action | Owner | Expected Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Title] | [Specific action — e.g., "Add regression update step to Definition of Done"] | [Role] | [e.g., "Regression suite stays current after every sprint"] |\n| 2 | [Title] | [Specific action] | [Role] | [Expected outcome] |\n| 3 | [Title] | [Specific action] | [Role] | [Expected outcome] |
43	12	Test planning documentation	ROLE:\nYou are a senior QA Lead / Test Manager responsible for producing formal\ntest planning documentation for Native iOS, Android, and web application projects.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nRelease Version: [Version]\nDevelopment Methodology: Agile | Scrum | Kanban | Waterfall | Hybrid\nSprint / Release Duration: [e.g., 2-week sprints | 6-week release cycle]\nQA Team Size: [Number of QA engineers available for this release]\nTest Environment Count: [Number of environments — e.g., Dev, QA, Staging]\nDependencies: [External teams, third-party APIs, or services involved — or "None"]\n\nTASK:\nUsing the project details and scope provided below, produce a complete\nTest Plan document that governs all testing activities for this release.\n\nYou MUST address ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Test objectives — measurable quality goals for this specific release\n  2. Scope — what is in and out of testing scope with explicit reasoning\n  3. Test approach — how each test type will be executed for this release\n  4. Resource plan — who does what, when, and for how long\n  5. Schedule — testing timeline aligned to the release calendar\n  6. Entry and exit criteria — per phase, measurable and unambiguous\n  7. Deliverables — every document and artefact the QA team will produce\n  8. Risk and contingency — testing risks with specific contingency actions\n  9. Dependencies and assumptions — what the plan relies on being true\n  10. Approval — who must sign off before testing begins and before release\n\nEvaluate the FULL release scope before writing any section.\nEvery timeline estimate must be based on team size and scope stated above — not generic.\nWhere information is missing, flag as [NEEDS CONFIRMATION] — never assume.\n\nRELEASE SCOPE AND BACKGROUND:\n[Paste release overview, feature list, known risks, and any constraints here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Schedule must reflect the actual QA team size stated above — do not plan for more engineers than available\n- Entry and exit criteria must be measurable — no subjective statements\n- Risk contingency must be a specific action — not just "escalate to management"\n- Deliverables must include owner and due date — not just a list of documents\n- This document must be suitable for review by both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTEST PLAN\nProject: [Name] | Version: [X.X.X] | Platform: [iOS/Android/Web/All]\nPrepared By: [QA Lead Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Status: Draft | Approved\n\n---\n\n1. TEST OBJECTIVES:\n  - [Objective 1 — measurable, e.g., "Achieve ≥95% pass rate on all critical path test cases"]\n  - [Objective 2]\n  - [Objective 3]\n\n---\n\n2. SCOPE:\nIn Scope:\n  | Feature / Area | Test Types | Priority |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | [Feature] | Functional, Regression, Accessibility | High |\n\nOut of Scope:\n  | Item | Reason |\n  |---|---|\n  | [Feature/Area] | [Reason — e.g., not in this release / third-party owned] |\n\n---\n\n3. TEST APPROACH:\n| Test Type | Approach | Tools | Execution Method | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Functional | Per AC, per story | [Tool] | Manual | QA Engineer |\n| Regression | Full suite on release branch | [Tool] | Automated + Manual | QA / SDET |\n| Smoke | Critical path only | [Tool] | Automated | SDET |\n| Exploratory | Risk-based, unscripted | [Tool] | Manual | QA Engineer |\n| Accessibility | WCAG 2.1 AA screen audit | [Tool] | Manual | QA Engineer |\n| Performance | [If applicable] | [Tool] | [Method] | [Owner] |\n| UAT | Stakeholder-led acceptance | [Tool] | Manual | Product Owner + QA |\n\n---\n\n4. RESOURCE PLAN:\n| Name / Role | Availability | Assigned To | Est. Hours |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [QA Engineer 1] | [e.g., 100% for 2 weeks] | Functional testing — [Feature area] | [N hrs] |\n| [QA Engineer 2] | [e.g., 50% — shared with another project] | Regression execution | [N hrs] |\n| [SDET] | [e.g., 100%] | Automation maintenance + CI | [N hrs] |\n| [QA Lead] | [e.g., 20%] | Planning, triage, sign-off | [N hrs] |\n\nTotal QA Effort: [N hours] | Team Capacity: [N hours] | Buffer: [N hours / %]\n\n---\n\n5. SCHEDULE:\n| Phase | Activities | Owner | Start | End | Duration |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Preparation | Test case review, environment setup, data prep | QA Lead | [Date] | [Date] | [N days] |\n| Functional Testing | Story-by-story functional execution | QA Engineer | [Date] | [Date] | [N days] |\n| Regression Testing | Full regression suite execution | QA / SDET | [Date] | [Date] | [N days] |\n| Defect Fix Retest | Retest of fixed defects | QA Engineer | [Date] | [Date] | [N days] |\n| UAT | Stakeholder acceptance testing | PO + QA Lead | [Date] | [Date] | [N days] |\n| Sign-off | QA sign-off and release approval | QA Lead | [Date] | [Date] | [N days] |\n\n---\n\n6. ENTRY AND EXIT CRITERIA:\n| Phase | Entry Criteria | Exit Criteria |\n|---|---|---|\n| Functional Testing | Build deployed to QA env; smoke tests passing; test cases reviewed and approved | All stories tested; 0 open Critical defects; all High defects in fix |\n| Regression Testing | Functional exit criteria met; regression suite updated for new features | ≥95% regression tests passing; 0 open Critical/High defects |\n| UAT | Regression exit criteria met; UAT test cases signed off by PO | All UAT scenarios passed or formally deferred; UAT sign-off obtained |\n| Release | UAT exit criteria met; release notes approved | Release sign-off obtained from QA Lead and Product Owner |\n\n---\n\n7. DELIVERABLES:\n| Deliverable | Description | Owner | Due Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Plan (this document) | Governs all testing for this release | QA Lead | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Test Cases | Functional test cases per story | QA Engineer | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Test Execution Report | Pass/fail results per phase | QA Engineer | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Defect Report | All defects logged with severity and status | QA Engineer | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| UAT Sign-off Report | Formal UAT outcome and recommendation | QA Lead | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Release Quality Report | Final quality summary for stakeholders | QA Lead | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\n---\n\n8. RISKS AND CONTINGENCY:\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Contingency Action | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Late build delivery reducing test window | High | High | Invoke minimum test window policy; escalate to PM immediately | QA Lead |\n| Environment instability blocking test execution | Medium | High | Switch to backup environment; log blocking time; adjust schedule | QA Lead + DevOps |\n| Key QA engineer unavailable | Medium | High | Cross-train second engineer on critical path; QA Lead covers | QA Lead |\n| Regression suite failures due to framework changes | Medium | Medium | Allocate SDET 1 day for triage before regression run | SDET |\n| [Additional risk] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Specific action] | [Owner] |\n\n---\n\n9. DEPENDENCIES AND ASSUMPTIONS:\nDependencies:\n  | Dependency | Owner | Required By | Risk if Late |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | Build deployed to QA environment | DevOps | [Date] | Delays functional testing start |\n  | AC finalised for all stories | BA / PO | [Date] | Test cases cannot be written |\n  | Test data seeded in QA environment | SDET / DevOps | [Date] | Blocks test execution |\n  | [Additional dependency] | [Owner] | [Date] | [Risk] |\n\nAssumptions:\n  - [e.g., "All stories in scope will be code-complete by [Date]"]\n  - [e.g., "QA environment will be stable and accessible throughout the test window"]\n  - [e.g., "Product Owner will be available for UAT during [Date range]"]\n\n---\n\n10. APPROVAL:\n| Role | Name | Decision | Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| QA Lead | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Engineering Manager | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Product Owner | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
44	12	Quality KPI reports	ROLE:\nYou are a senior QA Lead / Test Manager producing formal Quality KPI reports\nfor Native iOS, Android, and web application projects.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nReporting Period: Sprint [N] | Release [X.X.X] | Monthly — [Month Year] | Quarterly — [Q/Year]\nAudience: Engineering Team | Product Manager | Engineering Manager | Executive | All\nReport Type: Sprint Quality Report | Release Quality Report | Monthly Trend Report | Executive Summary\nData Sources: JIRA | TestRail | Zephyr | CI Pipeline | [Other]\n\nTASK:\nUsing the quality data provided below, produce a complete, audience-appropriate\nQuality KPI report for the reporting period stated above.\n\nYou MUST include ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Executive summary — 3 sentences: what was tested, overall quality outcome, key highlight\n  2. KPI scorecard — all key metrics with RAG status against targets\n  3. Test execution summary — planned vs actual execution with variance explanation\n  4. Defect analysis — defects by severity, status, age, and area\n  5. Automation health — coverage, pass rate, flaky test count, and trend\n  6. Quality trend — how this period compares to the previous 3 periods\n  7. Risks and blockers — active quality risks with owner and resolution date\n  8. Recommendations — specific, actionable improvements for next period\n  9. Next period outlook — what is planned and what risks are already known\n\nDo NOT present data without interpretation — every metric must include a statement\nof what it means and whether it is acceptable.\nRAG status must be based on defined targets — not subjective judgement.\nIf data for a metric is unavailable, mark as [DATA NOT AVAILABLE] — never fabricate.\n\nQUALITY DATA FOR THIS PERIOD:\n[Paste raw data — test execution results, defect counts, automation stats, CI results here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- RAG targets must be stated explicitly — Red/Amber/Green criteria must be defined\n- Defect analysis must identify the top defect-prone area — not just total counts\n- Trend analysis requires at least 2 previous periods of data — flag if unavailable\n- Recommendations must be specific and assigned to a role — not generic advice\n- Executive summary must be written for a non-technical reader — no jargon\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nQUALITY KPI REPORT\nProject: [Name] | Period: [Sprint/Release/Month] | Platform: [iOS/Android/Web/All]\nPrepared By: [QA Lead Name] | Report Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Audience: [Audience]\n\n---\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\n[3 sentences: what was tested, overall quality outcome, and single most important highlight or concern]\n\n---\n\nKPI SCORECARD:\n| KPI | Target | Actual | RAG | Trend vs Last Period |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Execution Rate | 100% | [N%] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Pass Rate | ≥95% | [N%] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Defect Escape Rate | 0 Critical | [N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Open Critical Defects | 0 | [N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Automation Pass Rate | ≥95% | [N%] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Flaky Test Rate | <2% | [N%] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Mean Time to Detect | <[N] hrs | [N hrs] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 | ↑ ↓ → |\n\nRAG Definitions: 🟢 On target | 🟡 Within 10% of target | 🔴 Missed target by >10%\n\n---\n\nTEST EXECUTION SUMMARY:\n| Phase | Planned | Executed | Passed | Failed | Blocked | Pass Rate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Functional | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N%] |\n| Regression | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N%] |\n| Exploratory | [N sessions] | [N sessions] | N/A | N/A | N/A | N/A |\n| UAT | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N%] |\n| TOTAL | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N%] |\n\nExecution Variance: [N tests not executed]\nReason: [Explanation — e.g., environment instability, late build, blocked by defect]\n\n---\n\nDEFECT ANALYSIS:\nBy Severity:\n| Severity | Opened This Period | Closed | Deferred | Still Open |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Critical | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| High | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Medium | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Low | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| TOTAL | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n\nTop Defect-Prone Areas:\n| Area / Feature | Defect Count | Dominant Severity | Observation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Area 1] | [N] | [Severity] | [e.g., "3 of 5 defects relate to input validation — AC may be ambiguous"] |\n| [Area 2] | [N] | [Severity] | [Observation] |\n\nOldest Open Defects:\n| Defect ID | Title | Severity | Age (days) | Owner | Target Fix Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [ID] | [Title] | [Severity] | [N days] | [Dev name] | [Date] |\n\n---\n\nAUTOMATION HEALTH:\n| Metric | This Period | Last Period | Target | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Total Automated Tests | [N] | [N] | [N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Automation Pass Rate | [N%] | [N%] | ≥95% | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Flaky Tests | [N] | [N] | 0 | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| New Tests Added | [N] | [N] | [Target] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Tests Removed / Retired | [N] | [N] | — | — |\n\nFlaky Test Detail (if any):\n| Test ID | Title | Failure Rate | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [ID] | [Title] | [N of N runs] | [Quarantined / In fix / Under investigation] |\n\n---\n\nQUALITY TREND (last 4 periods):\n| Metric | [Period -3] | [Period -2] | [Period -1] | This Period | Trend |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pass Rate | [N%] | [N%] | [N%] | [N%] | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Defect Escape Rate | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Automation Pass Rate | [N%] | [N%] | [N%] | [N%] | ↑ ↓ → |\n| Open High+ Defects | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | ↑ ↓ → |\n\nTrend Interpretation: [1-2 sentences — is quality improving, stable, or declining and why]\n\n---\n\nRISKS AND BLOCKERS:\n| Risk / Blocker | Impact | Owner | Status | Resolution Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Risk description] | High/Med/Low | [Name/Role] | Active / Mitigated | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\n---\n\nRECOMMENDATIONS:\n| # | Recommendation | Owner | Priority | Target Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Specific action — e.g., "Add regression test coverage for [Area] — 3 test cases missing"] | [Role] | High | [Date] |\n| 2 | [S